From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bind assignment expressions in generator expressions in the
 enclosing function

An assignment expression inside a generator expression binds its target in
the nearest scope that is not a comprehension, as CPython does. Nuitka made
the generator expression reach the name as a non-local, but when the
enclosing function did not assign the name anywhere else, there was no such
variable, and the look up silently found a module variable instead:

    def f(values):
        return tuple(x for v in values if (x := v))

left "x" in the module's globals, and every call of "f", from every thread,
shared one "x". Two threads could each yield the other's value.

The scope around the generator expressions is now asked for the variable, so
the non-local look up finds it there. A global or non-local declaration in
that function is respected as it is, and at module level that is the module
variable as before.

Offered upstream as https://github.com/Nuitka/Nuitka/pull/4069.

Signed-off-by: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
---

diff --git a/nuitka/tree/ReformulationAssignmentStatements.py b/nuitka/tree/ReformulationAssignmentStatements.py
index 4af479a..e3666c2 100644
--- a/nuitka/tree/ReformulationAssignmentStatements.py
+++ b/nuitka/tree/ReformulationAssignmentStatements.py
@@ -1201,6 +1201,18 @@ def buildNamedExprNode(provider, node, source_ref):
             (variable_name,), user_provided=False, source_ref=source_ref
         )
 
+        # The target belongs to the scope around the generator expressions,
+        # which needs to have the variable, or else the non-local look-up
+        # finds a module variable instead.
+        target_owner = locals_owner.getParentVariableProvider()
+        while target_owner.isExpressionOutlineFunction() or (
+            target_owner.isExpressionGeneratorObjectBody()
+            and target_owner.name == "<genexpr>"
+        ):
+            target_owner = target_owner.getParentVariableProvider()
+
+        target_owner.getVariableForAssignment(variable_name)
+
     statements = (
         makeStatementAssignmentVariable(
             variable=tmp_value, source=value, source_ref=source_ref
